 body=[('Why mills switch to one sizing powder',['A conventional size kitchen often blends PVA, starch, wax and several additives, each bought, stored and weighed separately. Every extra ingredient is another chance for a weighing error that shows up later as hairiness, breaks or uneven add-on on the loom.','EcoSize-CXW-111 is built to cut that complexity. The mill mixes one powder instead of a recipe of five or six, which simplifies stock control and makes the size box more consistent from shift to shift. For some quality counts a small top-up of other items may still help, and that is decided during the trial.']),
  ('Where it fits in your sizing line',['The powder is cooked and applied in the size box like any conventional size. It is used on cotton warp and on polyester blends such as PC and PV constructions. Indicative doses and savings from the owner\'s comparison sheet are shown in the technical tables below, and every recommendation is confirmed on your own sizing machine.'])],
 benefits=['Replaces all kinds of PVA and powder sizing chemicals','No separate starch, wax or polymer additions in most recipes','One-bag mixing for a simpler, more repeatable size kitchen','Good adhesion on polyester blends','Low foam in the size box'],
